            <profile name="Misfortune" id="c16d-a813-eb47-bbe7" hidden="false" typeId="7e20-258e-bf92-18f9" typeName="Ranged Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Ranged Weapon Strength" typeId="15aa-b6bd-6923-271f">Special</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Range Bands" typeId="be6a-50c6-d691-e2e9">2/4/6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Traits" typeId="3410-4428-ef91-eb61"/>
                <characteristic name="Specials" typeId="cdaf-b6ac-89d4-39ef"/>
                <characteristic name="Unique Effects" typeId="3bf8-6525-f003-4990">Successful attacks with this Weapon do no damage but the Target gains a Mishap Token.
Before a Damage Roll on a model with a Mishap Token, that model&apos;s Controller must flip a coin and call heads or tails.
If they call successfully, that model takes damage as normal, otherwise that model takes double damage.
After the damage roll, remove one Mishap Token.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
        <infoGroup name="Unique Effects" id="4043-3f5c-a3eb-9403" hidden="false">
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Lucky" id="7ae0-38f5-2e92-57f3" hidden="false" typeId="2f00-4eb0-a8cb-7022" typeName="Unique Effects">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="6de4-d067-c2aa-0dc2">While this model is in play, Friendly models may spend Luck Tokens to allow a Friendly model within 6&quot; to re-flip a coin.
Whenever an Effect causes dice to be re-rolled, this model gains 1 Ki Token.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
      </infoGroups>
